#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272105 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "969220db-a686-511b-b33a-0b4f6ab66b1a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16bb7c90-dd67-560d-bc55-0e6d60ffa1a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269459} {:answer/id #uuid "24f93a4c-04c3-5326-b385-3b237af5be9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -39 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269595} {:answer/id #uuid "45ce526b-cdce-5887-87fa-46e772b51158" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 5 \\\\ 39 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269907} {:answer/id #uuid "4d2b8368-af12-5270-8abb-2966b96811f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 39 \\\\ 8 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269962} {:answer/id #uuid "52a4f459-56be-5d2b-aa62-980c1e97fec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-39 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24f93a4c-04c3-5326-b385-3b237af5be9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -39 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269595} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f4347d9-b9dd-5363-a53a-02a14e4ccbbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271532}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac66a375-3ba5-552a-83b4-35e3ded13468" :question/math-academy-id "q-140482" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/db/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -39 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129697 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129155 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86028fae-a119-5194-975d-a6d9fad6faf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Given Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34b8c4b6-b53f-5fd6-8a59-c4c18583dd9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-25 & -14 \\\\ 16 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392233} {:answer/id #uuid "eaa442b6-3b37-5157-88fd-f23ac8a4d42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -18 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392234} {:answer/id #uuid "700fe7c1-5ebe-5a72-b683-b35432a45b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392235} {:answer/id #uuid "7362374a-a152-5b2b-adfe-f73b7788011b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -10 \\\\ -4 & 13\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392236} {:answer/id #uuid "991e6247-97fb-5467-ad97-075e201709bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & 6 \\\\ -20 & -11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eaa442b6-3b37-5157-88fd-f23ac8a4d42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -18 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392234} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ffe2e2a-b586-5e41-933b-844875782379" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392232}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ef695398-bdfe-5a30-85b6-97e0a8733294" :question/math-academy-id "q-38761" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,C=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the bases $B$ and $C$ of ${R}^{2},$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$, shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nFirst, let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of vectors from $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ To do this, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce $M$ using Gaussian elimination until we get the identity matrix on the left. By doing this, we obtain the required change-of-coordinates matrix on the right.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 11 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -5 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 11 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 11 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 7-2\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -18 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129130 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61bd0b4f-165c-5f31-b4ec-e0eff7e758e1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis Using a Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0609b365-00a9-5e3f-b18a-4ae8f0cb6423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 7 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395231} {:answer/id #uuid "900a056b-ff09-5fb7-93ec-d70236eeac1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395232} {:answer/id #uuid "5e60741c-2d26-5cbb-b653-d42461c6724c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395233} {:answer/id #uuid "a567a6a7-4ff1-59da-a544-576e1192accc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 9 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395234} {:answer/id #uuid "c2fc3385-8e0c-58d4-8ac0-fc0beafee826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & -1 \\\\ -8 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "900a056b-ff09-5fb7-93ec-d70236eeac1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395232} :answer-field/id #uuid "161f0cc1-c732-5e8a-bdbf-03f067c9d5be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "65dae103-c225-5d3f-8973-42e2dd0c3a80" :question/math-academy-id "q-97115" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{C}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $C$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $B.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/2e/2e82c232614bec8a98f079ea56d7913ee13e7b457e33e418198278d2e369fc5c.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}.\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{B}.$ Solving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot (-5)-3\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360754 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "969220db-a686-511b-b33a-0b4f6ab66b1a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "182077b4-5f2c-531e-96ce-4b88e8ab4d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 10 \\\\ -5 & 13\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357964} {:answer/id #uuid "42fae3bb-9ef9-579c-b81a-3be55f9c0d12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 16 \\\\ -11 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358324} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec1f99a-0977-5b71-97c0-662f0436dfd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 8 \\\\ -9 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358716} {:answer/id #uuid "be23d718-4726-5599-970d-363a78d2bd57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359411} {:answer/id #uuid "de1c3f3a-b06a-5be2-a7ff-4c20229cd2ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be23d718-4726-5599-970d-363a78d2bd57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359411} :answer-field/id #uuid "215bd893-15dc-5185-8467-98be175ac074" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "143b7701-47b4-58ee-98d5-de35b377edb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-97119" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/db/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot (-3)-(-1)\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395263 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129155 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86028fae-a119-5194-975d-a6d9fad6faf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Given Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f012443-8bd4-52ba-9493-3919a35ddba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395265} {:answer/id #uuid "47fce7e4-6451-5159-ab17-02eca79cf3cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395266} {:answer/id #uuid "77558324-5aee-52a7-9c40-5a51f9aaca4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -6 \\\\ 6 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395267} {:answer/id #uuid "9411351f-be5d-5884-a210-6d5c30bf0df5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395268} {:answer/id #uuid "3e925a83-495e-56e8-8d9b-c8d313746fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9411351f-be5d-5884-a210-6d5c30bf0df5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395268} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2c44b4f-f29e-547e-a303-1a31ffccb3ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "90dac6d1-6fdb-5236-89cf-8823a20cc32a" :question/math-academy-id "q-97281" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,C=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the bases $B$ and $C$ of ${R}^{2},$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$, shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nFirst, let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of vectors from $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ To do this, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce $M$ using Gaussian elimination until we get the identity matrix on the left. By doing this, we obtain the required change-of-coordinates matrix on the right.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-2)-(-3)\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
